# 13. HUMAN APPROVAL AND OUTBOUND COMMUNICATIONS

**NO UNAPPROVED AI-GENERATED EMAIL MAY BE SENT.**

Maintain the existing fail-closed approval architecture.

Workflow:

```text
Incoming Email
     ↓
AI Classification
     ↓
AI Draft Generation
     ↓
Human Review
     ↓
Edit / Approve / Reject
     ↓
Authorized Send
     ↓
Provider Delivery Result
     ↓
Sent Folder Reconciliation
     ↓
Audit Record
```

Required controls:

- Approver identity.
- Approval timestamp.
- Approved content version.
- Sender mailbox.
- Recipient list.
- Attachment references.
- Authorization record.
- Provider submission result.

Any material change to recipients, content, or attachments after approval must require reapproval.

A provider accepting a message does not prove delivery to the recipient's inbox.

Track submission, delivery evidence, bounces, and failures separately.

